# Win2Lin Linux Next Steps

Use this checklist after copying your Win2Lin export bundle to Linux and/or
running `scripts/Win2Lin.sh`. Work top-to-bottom; check items as you complete
them.

**Bundle path:** {{export_bundle_path}}
**Target distro / variant:** {{target_linux}}
**Restore mode used:** {{restore_mode}} (install / limited / restore-only / manual)
**Date:** {{next_steps_date}}

## Safety first

- [ ] I understand **passwords, browser cookies/session tokens, DPAPI-locked
      browser credentials, and private SSH/GPG keys were never copied**.
- [ ] I will **re-login** to accounts and recreate/move secrets only through
      secure, manual, user-approved steps.
- [ ] I reviewed the export location and report for sensitive path details
      before sharing.

## 1) Locate and inspect the bundle

- [ ] Confirm the bundle directory exists and is readable: `{{export_bundle_path}}`
- [ ] Check for expected files/folders (names vary by exporter version/mode):
  - [ ] `inventory.json`
  - [ ] `log.txt` and/or `robocopy_*.log` (lite)
  - [ ] `manifest.csv` / `copy_result.json` (advanced, if used)
  - [ ] `C_DRIVE/` (copied user/profile data, when present)
  - [ ] `D_DRIVE/` (copied additional drive data, when present)
- [ ] Skim logs for errors/warnings before assuming the copy is complete.

## 2) Restore safe files (review before applying)

If using `Win2Lin.sh`, follow its prompts and mode summary. If restoring
manually, copy only known-safe items.

- [ ] Restore reviewed `.gitconfig` / global gitignore (no embedded secrets)
- [ ] Restore selected dot-config directories with **no clobber** by default
- [ ] Restore fonts (user-level first if unsure)
- [ ] Restore **safe SSH files only**: `config`, `known_hosts`, `authorized_keys`,
      `*.pub`
- [ ] **Do not restore private keys** (`id_*` without `.pub`, GPG private
      material, token files) from the bundle; handle separately and securely

## 3) Re-login and account recovery

- [ ] Start browser and sign into sync (Brave/Edge/Chrome/Firefox as applicable)
- [ ] Sign into password manager / Google Password Manager
- [ ] Verify MFA/authenticator access and recovery options
- [ ] Sign into email, chat, cloud storage, and work accounts
- [ ] Sign into developer services (GitHub/GitLab/package registries/cloud CLIs)
      using fresh authentication

## 4) Reinstall apps (distro-appropriate)

Use `data/app-mappings/windows-to-linux.yml` and
`data/distro-packages/README.md` as guidance. **Respect distro mutability:**

- [ ] **Mutable distro:** install apps using the normal package manager; review
      commands before running; accept prompts consciously.
- [ ] **Immutable/atomic/transactional/declarative/managed distro:** **do not
      auto-mutate the system**. Prefer Flatpak, distrobox/toolbox, or documented
      manual workflows (rpm-ostree/MicroOS transactional/NixOS/Guix/Vanilla OS
      guidance as applicable).

Apps to install/verify:

- [ ] Browser(s): {{browser_plan}}
- [ ] Communication: {{communication_plan}}
- [ ] Office/documents: {{office_plan}}
- [ ] Media/utilities: {{utilities_plan}}
- [ ] Development tools: {{dev_tools_plan}}

## 5) Rebuild development environment

- [ ] Install Git and verify identity/signing settings
- [ ] Create or securely install SSH keys; test `ssh -T` / remote access
- [ ] Install Node/Python/Go versions required by your projects
- [ ] Recreate environments from manifests/lockfiles (no `node_modules`, no
      Windows `.venv` copies)
- [ ] Install Docker/Podman using a method supported by your distro
- [ ] Recreate `.env`/secrets locally and securely (never copy old secrets
      blindly)
- [ ] Run project smoke tests/builds

## 6) Validate data and workflows

- [ ] Open critical documents/spreadsheets/presentations and check formatting
- [ ] Verify photos, videos, archives, and downloads are intact
- [ ] Confirm important project repositories build/run/test
- [ ] Check printers, audio, camera, screen sharing, VPN, and peripherals
- [ ] Confirm cloud sync/backup behavior is what you expect (avoid accidental
      duplicate uploads/conflicts)

## 7) Clean-up and fallback

- [ ] Keep the export bundle on a safe backup until migration is verified
- [ ] Keep Windows available for 1–2 weeks if dual-booting or uncertain
- [ ] Record unresolved issues in `templates/migration-report.md.tmpl` or your
      migration notes
- [ ] After confidence is high, plan secure cleanup of temporary exports/copies
      (do not rush disk wipes)

